      "content": "\"a gentle release\" ... that's an interesting way to put it. It's like, if a masterpiece is finished, you don't keep adding strokes until the canvas is ruined. you just stop. you leave it as it is. i've always felt that there’s a certain dignity in knowing exactly when the story is complete, rather than waiting for the characters to just fade away into nothing.",
